@api = http://localhost:5123

# The same bank, three APIs. REST and GraphQL below; gRPC (http://localhost:5250, HTTP/2) is played with the comparison
# client: dotnet run --project Styles.Client (the HTTP clients of VS and VS Code do not speak gRPC).

# ─── REST: resources, verbs, statuses ───

### A resource and the addresses of the linked resources (_links)
GET {{api}}/customers/alice

### The accounts: a complete representation, the same for everyone (IBAN, owner, links… even if the screen does not want them)
GET {{api}}/customers/alice/accounts

### The operations: one more request PER account (the "1 + N")
GET {{api}}/accounts/10001/operations?limit=3

### An account, with its ETag (run again with If-None-Match: 304 without body as long as nothing changes)
GET {{api}}/accounts/10001

### … the same request with the received ETag: 304 Not Modified, without body
GET {{api}}/accounts/10001
If-None-Match: "10001-v6"

### Create a transfer: 201 Created + Location
POST {{api}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "10001", "target": "20001", "amount": 25.50, "label": "Cinema" }

### An error: an HTTP status (422) and an application/problem+json body
POST {{api}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "20001", "target": "10001", "amount": 1000000 }

# ─── GraphQL: one address, the client writes its query ───

### The whole home screen in one query: exactly the fields displayed
POST {{api}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "{ customer(id: \"alice\") { name accounts { label balance operations(latest: 3) { date label amount } } } }" }

### With variables, and the same field twice thanks to aliases
POST {{api}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query ($a: ID!, $b: ID!) { current: account(number: $a) { balance } savings: account(number: $b) { balance } }",
  "variables": { "a": "10001", "b": "10002" }
}

### An error: 200 anyway, the data at null, the error in "errors" (with its path and its code)
POST {{api}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "{ a: account(number: \"10001\") { label } b: account(number: \"99999\") { label } }" }

### A mutation
POST {{api}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "mutation { makeTransfer(source: \"10001\", target: \"20001\", amount: 10) { id source { balance } } }" }

### Refused before execution: too deep (limit: 6 levels)
POST {{api}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "{ customer(id: \"alice\") { accounts { owner { accounts { owner { accounts { label } } } } } } }" }

### The published contract (SDL), with the deprecated field
GET {{api}}/graphql/schema

### Which fields do the clients ask for? (enough to know when to remove "balanceText")
GET {{api}}/graphql/usage

# ─── Behind the scenes ───

### How many "database" reads of the operations (one per account with REST, one in all with GraphQL and gRPC)
GET {{api}}/statistics
